From be9b8548b44487440dbbcd4aff0472396a2af107 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:36:06 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] PlaitOS: SettingsLib in the PlaitOS look

Settings and every other screen built on SettingsLib's expressive theme
follow plait-design:
- Groups: 14 dp corners, square inner corners, no gap between the rows of a
  group and a hairline between them that starts where the text starts
  (MarginItemDecoration; SettingsPreferenceGroupAdapter.isGroupedWithNext).
  The space between groups stays.
- Main switch: a 14 dp card tinted with the accent (primary at 16%) instead
  of the solid container, text in the normal colour.
- Switches: a plain thumb, no check or cross.
- Header: a plain back arrow (Material Symbols Rounded arrow_back) instead
  of the filled circle, 24 dp titles.
- Section labels in muted text (on-surface-variant) instead of the accent.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
